as expected the cincinnati bengals made  lsu quarterback joe burrow the number  one overall pick in the 2020 draft there  was an effort by the dolphins to make  the move from number five to number one  we don't yet know what if anything  concrete was offered there were various  ideas that were percolating out there  the question of whether or not the  dolphins could offer cash to the bengals  and we know how extremely careful the  bengals are with money and how they  value money but there is a long-standing  nfl policy that for player drafts  or for player trades rather money cannot  be part of the equation i actually heard  that there was a thought that maybe the  dolphins could take the fifth overall  pick pay his signing bonus and then  trade into the dolphins or to the  bengals rather with the signing bonus  already paid by the dolphins and then  pick up joe burrows contract and pay his  signing bonus in full contract that  gives you an idea of the kind of  creativity and outside the box thinking  that was going on this wasn't some  idle  issue by the dolphins where they just  kicked the tires and maybe thought about  trying to do it they wanted to do it the  bengals said no and maybe one of these  days we'll find out exactly what the  dolphins offered to get joe burrow but  for the bengals who kept joe burrow he  becomes the future what will he do with  andy dalton will joe burroughs start  right away can they put enough around  him to turn the bengals into a contender  they haven't won a playoff game since  january of 1991 and now with joe burrow  it's a new era for the bengals and we'll  see if they can turn things around in  cincinnati we'll be back all night long  with more reaction to picks made during  the 2020 nfl draft  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports
 

